# TODO - CUDA exact VM adapter

## Objective

Implement the first GPU adapter with exact discrete Malbolge semantics and
massively parallel independent VM execution for candidate evaluation and test
batches.

## Acceptance

- CUDA kernels implement exact discrete VM semantics for independent batches and
  are differentially checked against the CPU reference across randomized and
  boundary-heavy corpora.
- A CPU/reference path remains sufficient for correctness, and accelerator
  failure/unavailability changes performance rather than semantic acceptance.
- The declared scope contains no unresolved placeholder implementation or
  undocumented workaround required for this objective to function.
- Evidence is durable enough to move this TODO to `docs/todo/completed/` and
  remove the exact TODO heading without losing unfinished intent.

## Evidence

- Expected durable artifact surface: `accelerator/`, `algorithms/`,
  `optimizer/`, `benchmarks/accelerator/`, `tests/optimizer/`.
- Required evidence: CPU/reference differential results, device/resource
  metadata, failure/fallback tests, and benchmark samples for claimed speedups.
- Active foundation: integer-only CUDA kernels implement exact classic
  rotate/crazy batches through NVRTC + Driver API behind the shared accelerator
  port. CUDA 13.3 Update 1 redistributables are reproducibly pinned by component
  path/version/SHA-256; the active Python adapter uses standard-library `ctypes`
  only.
- Compact classic one-step VM execution is now active. A fixed-width request
  declares registers/counters/input plus at most four keyed memory cells; CUDA
  returns the full `StepTrace`-equivalent projection. Rust integration compares
  fourteen instruction/edge fixtures directly with normative
  `Machine::step_traced()`, including atomic rejection and write aliasing.
- RTX 4060 (`sm_89`) development evidence matches CPU primitive results and Rust
  classic-step traces. Resident full-memory multi-step VM execution, adaptive
  resource sizing, current-profile coverage, and performance evidence remain
  open.
- Prerequisite completion evidence: `replaceable-accelerator-boundary`,
  `batch-vm-execution`.
